</div><p class="section-intro">The AMF Memorandum v2.0 first sets out the technical facts and functional perimeter of Osnias Clearing. It describes a canonical clearing register on Sei, clearing tokens governed by strict invariants, a non-custodial operating model, and an explicit separation between the calculation of obligations, the custody of assets and their final settlement.</p><p class="section-intro">The document then details the external escrow architecture and the allocation of responsibilities between Osnias Clearing and node operators. It covers fail-closed controls, the 1:1 chamber-level invariant, the absence of a governance token, and the absence of asset custody by Osnias, in order to distinguish the clearing infrastructure from custody and settlement functions.</p><p class="section-intro">Finally, the memorandum sets out the main regulatory qualification questions to be examined with the AMF as part of a preliminary regulatory dialogue. Its purpose is to obtain legal guidance on the system under MiCA and the applicable framework before developing a testnet pilot with a partner established in France, without prejudging any final legal qualification.</p>
